      asl3: { role: "重大な危険能力のしきい値を超えたモデル向けの強化レベル。より厳格な統制が必須。", tech: "強化されたデプロイ統制、セキュリティ強化、内部脅威対策。", biz: "高能力モデルほど統制を先に固める。ここを軽視すると事故の爆風半径が跳ね上がる。", qa: "ASL-3で何が変わる？（→デプロイ統制とセキュリティ統制の両方が強化必須に）", cost: "統制コストは上がるが、能力に見合う安全対価として正当化できる。", roleEn: "An elevated level for models crossing serious dangerous-capability thresholds. Stricter controls are mandatory.", techEn: "Hardened deployment controls, enhanced security, insider-threat mitigations.", bizEn: "The more capable the model, the earlier you lock down controls. Neglect here spikes the blast radius.", qaEn: "What changes at ASL-3? (→ both deployment and security controls must be strengthened)", costEn: "Control cost rises but is justified as the price matching capability." },
      deploy: { role: "モデルの出力・挙動を制御する統制。脱獄耐性・有害出力防止・悪用検知。", tech: "分類器、熟慮的アラインメント、出力フィルタ、悪用モニタリング。", biz: "「モデルが何を出すか」の統制。ユーザー向けリスクの主戦場。", qa: "デプロイ統制の要は？（→脱獄耐性と悪用検知の両立、過剰拒否の回避）", cost: "分類器・モニタリングのコスト。安全の直接投資。", roleEn: "Controls governing the model's outputs/behavior: jailbreak robustness, harmful-output prevention, misuse detection.", techEn: "Classifiers, deliberative alignment, output filters, misuse monitoring.", bizEn: "Governing 'what the model emits.' The main arena for user-facing risk.", qaEn: "The crux of deployment controls? (→ balance jailbreak robustness and misuse detection, avoid over-refusal)", costEn: "Cost of classifiers/monitoring. A direct safety investment." },
      secure: { role: "モデルの重み・学習環境を守る統制。窃取・内部脅威からモデルそのものを保護。", tech: "重みアクセス制御、内部脅威対策、サプライチェーン保護、隔離環境。", biz: "「モデルが盗まれない」統制。高能力モデルほど窃取の標的価値が上がる。", qa: "セキュリティ統制の焦点は？（→重みの窃取防止と内部脅威対策）", cost: "隔離・アクセス制御の固定費。能力段階に応じて上げる。", roleEn: "Controls protecting model weights and the training environment from theft and insider threats.", techEn: "Weight-access control, insider-threat mitigation, supply-chain protection, isolated environments.", bizEn: "Governing 'the model can't be stolen.' The more capable, the higher its theft value.", qaEn: "Focus of security controls? (→ preventing weight theft and mitigating insider threats)", costEn: "Fixed cost of isolation/access control; raise it with the capability tier." },
      redteam: { role: "敵対的テストで統制の穴を突く。デプロイ前の保証プロセスの核。", tech: "敵対的プロンプト、脱獄試行、サボタージュ評価、外部レッドチーム。", biz: "「投入前にわざと壊す」投資。壊れてから気づくより桁で安い。", qa: "レッドチームで何を見る？（→統制の回避可能性、想定外の危険挙動）", cost: "外部レッドチーム含めコストはかかるが、事故回避の保険。", roleEn: "Adversarial testing that probes control gaps. The core of pre-deployment assurance.", techEn: "Adversarial prompts, jailbreak attempts, sabotage evals, external red teams.", bizEn: "An investment to 'deliberately break it before launch.' Orders cheaper than noticing after.", qaEn: "What does red-teaming look for? (→ control-bypass potential, unexpected dangerous behavior)", costEn: "Costs (incl. external teams) but is insurance against incidents." },
      gate: { role: "全統制を通過して初めてリリースを許可する最終ゲート。能力段階に応じた段階導入。", tech: "リリース判断基準、段階的ロールアウト、カナリア、ロールバック計画。", biz: "「投入して良いか」の最終判断。高能力ほど監督を固めてから広げる。", qa: "リリースゲートの判断軸は？（→統制の充足、レッドチーム結果、段階導入計画）", cost: "ゲートは遅延を生むが、一括投入の事故コストより遥かに安い。", roleEn: "The final gate that permits release only after all controls pass. Phased rollout per capability tier.", techEn: "Release criteria, staged rollout, canary, rollback plan.", bizEn: "The final 'is it OK to ship' call. The more capable, the more you lock down oversight before scaling.", qaEn: "Decision axes of the release gate? (→ control sufficiency, red-team results, phased-rollout plan)", costEn: "The gate adds delay but is far cheaper than the incident cost of all-at-once launch." }
