// ============ 企業研究: 面接タイプ別プレイブック ============
const INTERVIEW_PLAYBOOK = [
  {"type":"システムデザイン","typeEn":"System Design","weight":"全社共通で最重要","weightEn":"Most important across all","flow":"要件確認 → 概算（規模・コスト・レイテンシ）→ 構成図 → 深掘り → トレードオフ","flowEn":"Clarify requirements → estimate (scale, cost, latency) → draw architecture → deep dive → trade-offs","win":"「まず要件を確認させてください」で始め、数値を宣言して概算し、選んだ理由と捨てた選択肢を語る。","winEn":"Open with 'let me first clarify requirements,' declare numbers and estimate, then explain what you chose and rejected.","trap":"いきなり構成を描き始める／トレードオフを語らず『正解』を1つだけ出す。","trapEn":"Jumping straight into drawing / giving one 'right answer' without discussing trade-offs.","drill":"図面道場で構成を口頭再現→概算ドリルで数値の所作→設計判断バトルで『なぜこちらか』を反復。","drillEn":"Reproduce architectures aloud in Diagrams → practice numbers in Estimation → drill 'why this one' in Trade-offs."},
  {"type":"行動面接（STAR）","typeEn":"Behavioral (STAR)","weight":"Amazon（LP）で最重要","weightEn":"Most important at Amazon (LP)","flow":"状況(S) → 課題(T) → 自分の行動(A) → 結果・数値(R) → 学び","flowEn":"Situation → Task → your Action → Result/numbers → learning","win":"『私は』で語り、定量成果（%・金額・期間）と自分固有の貢献を必ず入れる。","winEn":"Speak in 'I,' and always include quantified results (%, money, time) and your specific contribution.","trap":"『チームで』に逃げて自分の役割が消える／結果が定性的で数字がない。","trapEn":"Hiding behind 'we, as a team' so your role vanishes / qualitative results with no numbers.","drill":"STARストーリーを10本、数値付きで事前に文章化。LP16項目に案件をマッピング。","drillEn":"Write out 10 STAR stories with numbers in advance. Map your projects to the 16 Leadership Principles."},
  {"type":"AI戦略ケース","typeEn":"AI Strategy Case","weight":"コンサル出身の主戦場","weightEn":"A consultant's home turf","flow":"課題の構造化 → 選択肢の列挙 → 評価軸の設定 → 推奨 → リスクと次の一手","flowEn":"Structure the problem → enumerate options → set evaluation axes → recommend → risks and next move","win":"Build vs Buy・モデル選定・レガシー移行等で、評価軸を先に置き数字で推奨する。","winEn":"For Build vs Buy, model selection, legacy migration, etc., set evaluation axes first and recommend with numbers.","trap":"技術の話に閉じてビジネスインパクトが消える／逆に精神論で技術的裏付けがない。","trapEn":"Getting lost in tech so business impact disappears / or all inspiration with no technical grounding.","drill":"設計判断バトルの各テーマを『5分で推奨まで語る』練習。Key numbersで数字の裏付けを仕込む。","drillEn":"Practice taking each Trade-offs topic 'to a recommendation in 5 minutes.' Load numeric backing from Key numbers."},
  {"type":"カルチャーフィット","typeEn":"Culture Fit","weight":"全社（各社固有）","weightEn":"All companies (each specific)","flow":"各社の価値観（Googleyness / LP / Growth Mindset等）に自分の経験を接続","flowEn":"Connect your experience to each company's values (Googleyness / LP / Growth Mindset, etc.)","win":"各社の行動規範を1つ選び、それを体現した具体エピソードを1分で語れるようにする。","winEn":"Pick one of a company's behavioral norms and be able to tell a specific story embodying it in one minute.","trap":"価値観を暗唱するだけでエピソードがない／どの会社にも同じ話をする。","trapEn":"Just reciting the values with no story / telling the same story to every company.","drill":"企業研究タブの各社『フィット分析』を読み、自分の案件と接続する1文を用意。","drillEn":"Read each company's 'Fit analysis' in the Companies tab and prepare one sentence connecting it to your work."},
  {"type":"コーディング面接","typeEn":"Coding Interview","weight":"SWE・ML Engineer・Applied AI Engineer で最重要。フロント/バックエンド問わずソフトウェア職の一次関門。","weightEn":"Most critical for SWE, ML Engineer, and Applied AI Engineer; the first gate for nearly all software roles regardless of frontend or backend focus.","flow":"問題提示 → 要件・制約の確認 → 素朴解の合意 → 計算量の見積り → 最適化方針の口頭説明 → 実装 → テストケースでの動作確認 → 追加質問（拡張・エッジケース）","flowEn":"Problem statement → clarify requirements and constraints → agree on a brute-force baseline → estimate complexity → verbalize an optimization plan → implement → walk through test cases → follow-ups (extensions and edge cases)","win":"コードを書く前に入出力例で仕様を固定し、時間/空間計算量を宣言してから実装する。詰まったら黙らず思考を実況し、面接官をペアの相方として使う。","winEn":"Lock the spec with concrete I/O examples before typing, declare time/space complexity up front, and narrate your reasoning aloud so the interviewer works with you as a pair when you get stuck.","trap":"最適解を焦って書き始め、要件確認を飛ばして誤った問題を解く。エッジケース（空・重複・オーバーフロー）とテストを最後まで放置する。","trapEn":"Rushing straight to the optimal solution, skipping clarification and solving the wrong problem, and leaving edge cases (empty, duplicates, overflow) and tests untouched until it is too late.","drill":"開発・言語道場でアルゴリズムとデータ構造を反復し、概算ドリルで計算量を口頭で即答する訓練を積む。","drillEn":"Drill algorithms and data structures in the Dev/Language Dojo, and use the Estimation Drill to snap out complexity analysis aloud on demand."},
  {"type":"ML System Design（ML設計深掘り）","typeEn":"ML System Design","weight":"ML Engineer・Applied AI Engineer・MLOps で重い。モデルだけでなくデータ・学習・提供・監視まで一気通貫で問われる。","weightEn":"Heavy for ML Engineer, Applied AI Engineer, and MLOps roles; probes the full pipeline from data and training through serving and monitoring, not just the model.","flow":"ビジネス目標の確認 → 問題の定式化（分類/回帰/ランキング等） → 評価指標の設計 → データとラベルの入手 → 特徴量とモデル選定 → 学習・提供アーキテクチャ → オンライン/オフライン評価 → 監視・再学習・ドリフト対策","flowEn":"Confirm the business goal → frame the problem (classification/regression/ranking) → design evaluation metrics → source data and labels → choose features and models → design training and serving architecture → online/offline evaluation → monitoring, retraining, and drift handling","win":"ビジネス指標とML指標を明示的に結び付け、オフライン評価とオンラインA/Bを分けて語る。データの偏り・ラベル遅延・フィードバックループなど運用リスクを自分から挙げる。","winEn":"Explicitly tie business metrics to ML metrics, separate offline evaluation from online A/B testing, and proactively surface operational risks like data skew, label latency, and feedback loops.","trap":"モデルの精度議論に偏り、データ品質・提供レイテンシ・監視を軽視する。指標を決めずに手法から入る。","trapEn":"Over-indexing on model accuracy while neglecting data quality, serving latency, and monitoring, and diving into techniques before defining the metric.","drill":"設計判断バトルで指標・データ・提供のトレードオフを言語化し、図面道場でパイプライン全体を1枚に描く練習をする。","drillEn":"Use the Design Decision Battle to verbalize metric/data/serving trade-offs, and the Diagram Dojo to sketch the whole pipeline on a single canvas."},
  {"type":"テイクホーム課題","typeEn":"Take-Home Assignment","weight":"スタートアップ・Data Scientist・Applied AI で多い。数時間〜数日で完成度と判断力を総合評価される。","weightEn":"Common at startups and for Data Scientist and Applied AI roles; evaluates completeness and judgment over a few hours to a few days.","flow":"課題受領 → スコープと前提の宣言 → データ探索/設計 → 実装 → 検証とテスト → README/レポート作成 → 提出 → レビュー面談での深掘り","flowEn":"Receive the prompt → declare scope and assumptions → explore data or design → implement → validate and test → write the README/report → submit → deep-dive in the review interview","win":"スコープを自分で切り、割り切った点を README に明記する。動くこと・読めること・再現できることを優先し、なぜその設計にしたかの意思決定を短く残す。","winEn":"Cut scope deliberately and document the trade-offs in the README, prioritize code that runs, reads clearly, and reproduces, and leave a short record of why you made each design decision.","trap":"完璧主義で時間超過し未完成のまま提出。派手な機能に走り、テスト・ドキュメント・再現手順を欠く。","trapEn":"Overrunning on perfectionism and submitting something unfinished, chasing flashy features while omitting tests, documentation, and reproduction steps.","drill":"設計判断バトルでスコープ切りとトレードオフの説明を鍛え、開発・言語道場で読みやすい実装とテストの型を作る。","drillEn":"Sharpen scoping and trade-off articulation in the Design Decision Battle, and build habits for readable implementation and tests in the Dev/Language Dojo."},
  {"type":"ライブコーディング/ペアプロ","typeEn":"Live Coding / Pair Programming","weight":"SWE・Forward Deployed Engineer で重い。実務に近い環境で協働性とデバッグ力を見られる。","weightEn":"Heavy for SWE and Forward Deployed Engineer roles; assesses collaboration and debugging ability in a near-real work setting.","flow":"課題とリポジトリ提示 → 既存コードの読解 → 変更方針の合意 → 小さく実装しながら実行 → テストで確認 → リファクタ → 面接官との対話で改善","flowEn":"Present the task and repo → read the existing code → agree on an approach → implement in small runnable steps → verify with tests → refactor → improve through dialogue with the interviewer","win":"こまめに実行して赤→緑を刻み、意図を声に出す。面接官の提案を素直に取り込み、行き詰まりも協働で解く姿勢を見せる。","winEn":"Run frequently to move red to green in small steps, think aloud about intent, take the interviewer's suggestions gracefully, and show you resolve blockers collaboratively.","trap":"沈黙して一人で抱え込む。実行せず頭の中だけで長く書き、環境やツールの使い方でつまずく。","trapEn":"Going silent and hoarding the problem, writing long stretches in your head without running anything, and fumbling with the environment or tooling.","drill":"開発・言語道場で実行→テスト→リファクタのループを体に入れ、設計判断バトルで対話しながら方針を変える練習をする。","drillEn":"Internalize the run-test-refactor loop in the Dev/Language Dojo, and practice changing course through dialogue in the Design Decision Battle."},
  {"type":"提案・プレゼン（顧客/技術提案）","typeEn":"Proposal / Presentation (Customer or Technical Pitch)","weight":"Solutions Architect・Sales Engineer・AI Consultant で最重要。技術を意思決定者に伝え動かす力を測る。","weightEn":"Most critical for Solutions Architect, Sales Engineer, and AI Consultant roles; measures the ability to convey technology to decision-makers and drive action.","flow":"課題設定の共有 → 顧客の状況/制約のヒアリング → 提案の全体像 → アーキテクチャ/アプローチの説明 → 効果・コスト・リスク → 次のステップ → 質疑応答","flowEn":"Share the framing → hear the customer's context and constraints → present the overall proposal → explain the architecture/approach → cover value, cost, and risk → define next steps → handle Q&A","win":"結論から話し、聞き手の言葉でビジネス価値を語る。トレードオフとリスクを正直に示し、次アクションを具体化して意思決定を促す。","winEn":"Lead with the conclusion, frame business value in the audience's language, present trade-offs and risks honestly, and make next steps concrete to prompt a decision.","trap":"技術詳細を並べて価値が伝わらない。想定質問への準備不足で反論に崩れ、時間配分を誤る。","trapEn":"Piling on technical detail so the value never lands, being underprepared for objections, and mismanaging the time budget.","drill":"設計判断バトルで意思決定者向けの説明とトレードオフの言語化を鍛え、図面道場で1枚絵の提案図を作る。","drillEn":"Rehearse decision-maker-facing explanation and trade-off articulation in the Design Decision Battle, and build one-page proposal visuals in the Diagram Dojo."},
  {"type":"総合評価（Bar Raiser型）","typeEn":"Holistic Evaluation (Bar Raiser)","weight":"大手テック全般で最終判断に効く。特定スキルより一貫性・基準の高さ・採用可否の総合判断を担う。","weightEn":"Decisive in final calls across big tech; less about a single skill and more about consistency, raising the bar, and the overall hire/no-hire judgment.","flow":"幅広い経歴の確認 → 深掘り質問で一貫性を検証 → 価値観・判断基準の確認 → 難所での意思決定の掘り下げ → 反証質問 → 総合所見","flowEn":"Review a broad background → probe deeply to test consistency → check values and decision principles → dig into judgment at hard moments → challenge with counter-questions → form a holistic assessment","win":"一つの実績を複数角度から深掘りされても事実ベースで一貫させる。失敗と学びを率直に語り、判断基準を明確に持つ。","winEn":"Keep a single accomplishment consistent and fact-based under multi-angle probing, speak candidly about failures and lessons, and hold clear decision principles.","trap":"話を盛って深掘りで矛盾が露呈する。曖昧な一般論に逃げ、自分の判断と役割を語れない。","trapEn":"Embellishing until deep probing exposes contradictions, hiding in vague generalities, and failing to articulate your own judgment and role.","drill":"設計判断バトルで自分の意思決定を反証質問に耐える形に鍛え、行動面接系のドリルで実績エピソードの一貫性を検証する。","drillEn":"Harden your decisions against counter-questions in the Design Decision Battle, and stress-test the consistency of your accomplishment stories with behavioral drills."},
  {"type":"ハンズオン/PoCデモ","typeEn":"Hands-On / PoC Demo","weight":"Customer Engineer・Sales Engineer・Forward Deployed Engineer で重い。実際に動くものを作って見せる力を測る。","weightEn":"Heavy for Customer Engineer, Sales Engineer, and Forward Deployed Engineer roles; measures the ability to build and show something that actually works.","flow":"ユースケース設定 → 環境/データ準備 → 最小構成のPoC実装 → デモシナリオ設計 → デモ実施 → 制約と本番化への道筋の説明 → 質疑","flowEn":"Define the use case → prepare environment and data → build a minimal PoC → design the demo scenario → run the demo → explain limitations and the path to production → Q&A","win":"『動く』ことを最短で示し、失敗しても回復できるデモ設計にする。PoCと本番の差分（スケール・セキュリティ・運用）を先回りして語る。","winEn":"Show something working by the shortest path, design the demo to recover gracefully from failures, and get ahead of the PoC-to-production gap (scale, security, operations).","trap":"作り込みすぎて当日に動かない。デモ環境依存の裏技に頼り、本番化の課題を語れない。","trapEn":"Over-building so it fails on the day, relying on demo-environment tricks, and being unable to speak to what productionization requires.","drill":"開発・言語道場で最小構成を素早く組む反復をし、図面道場でPoCから本番構成への差分を図解する。","drillEn":"Practice standing up minimal builds fast in the Dev/Language Dojo, and diagram the PoC-to-production delta in the Diagram Dojo."},
  {"type":"リーダーシップ・マネジメント面接","typeEn":"Leadership / Management Interview","weight":"TPM・PM・EM・リード職で最重要。人と組織を動かし成果を出すマネジメント力を測る。","weightEn":"Most critical for TPM, PM, EM, and lead roles; measures the ability to move people and organizations to deliver results.","flow":"リーダー経験の確認 → チーム/組織の状況説明 → 難所での意思決定の深掘り → コンフリクト対応・人の育成 → 成果と学び → 価値観の確認","flowEn":"Review leadership experience → describe the team/org situation → dig into decisions at hard moments → conflict handling and people development → results and lessons → values check","win":"自分の判断と他者への影響を主語を『私』で語りつつ、成果はチームに帰属させる。対立・低評価者対応・優先順位付けを具体エピソードで示す。","winEn":"Speak in the first person about your own decisions and influence while crediting results to the team, and illustrate conflict, underperformer handling, and prioritization with concrete stories.","trap":"『私たち』だけで語り自分の貢献が見えない。理想論に終始し、難しい人・対立・失敗のリアルな話を出せない。","trapEn":"Speaking only in 'we' so your own contribution disappears, staying idealistic, and failing to bring real stories about difficult people, conflict, and failure.","drill":"設計判断バトルで組織的な意思決定を反証に耐える形に鍛え、行動面接系ドリルでリーダーシップの実績エピソードを型化する。","drillEn":"Harden organizational decisions against challenge in the Design Decision Battle, and template your leadership stories with behavioral drills."}
];

